{
  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "[P2] Surface systemic GitHub query failures",
      "body": "When GitHub authentication expires or network/rate-limit failures affect these queries, `|| true` converts every failure into empty JSON, after which the script merely increments `skipped` and exits successfully. In standalone or `--drift-only` runs, `tri-daily` therefore discards the diagnostics and the scheduler treats an inactive patrol as healthy; preserve enough error information to return nonzero for systemic failures.",
      "confidence_score": 0.96,
      "priority": 2,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/var/home/matt/dev/mybd/.worktrees/mybd/issue-drift-timer/scripts/tri-drift",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 95,
          "end": 100
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Propagate failures from the worklist reader",
      "body": "When `bd list` or the worklist's `jq` pipeline fails, its process-substitution status is not propagated to the parent `while`; the loop simply reads no rows and the script reports `Flagged 0 ...` with exit status 0. This makes tracker/database failures indistinguishable from a legitimate empty worklist, so capture and validate the worklist before iterating.",
      "confidence_score": 0.98,
      "priority": 2,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/var/home/matt/dev/mybd/.worktrees/mybd/issue-drift-timer/scripts/tri-drift",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 132,
          "end": 132
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "overall_correctness": "patch is incorrect",
  "overall_explanation": "The drift patrol can silently report success when either its local worklist or upstream GitHub queries fail. Because this is intended for unattended scheduling, those false-success paths materially undermine failure detection.",
  "overall_confidence_score": 0.97
}

